Given the number of C tools you're building (minifetch, gitprompt, ftree, shamir, vaultcrypt), your install.sh is starting to look like a build system.

It might be cleaner to move all those cc calls into a single Makefile in the scripts/ directory. Then, your install.sh simply calls:

Bash
section "Compiling C Tools"
run_cmd make -C "$DOTFILES_DIR/scripts" install PREFIX="$TARGET_HOME/bin"
This separates installation (shell) from compilation (make).
